BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cosplay Camp Summer Camp Jul 13-17 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T160000
UID:ttl-10932862812353@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Cosplay and LARP \n\n \n \n Recommended Ages 8-13 \n \n \n\n \
 n \n \n At the TTL Makerspace we believe that learning should be fun\, saf
 e and fun! \n\n \n We will begin the week with a study of design before d
 ividing in to two or more teams both deciding what kind of theme they want
  to cosplay. We will design our cosplay\, create it as well as personalize
  it. With a heavy emphasis on safety\, we will empower kids with the confi
 dence and skills needed to use tools and equipment in a community makerspa
 ce.\n\n \n \n We will learn to design and build a cosplay incorporating se
 wing\, Leatherworking\, Woodworking\,3d printing\, laser cutting and elect
 ronics.\n\n \n \n Note: Cosplay can be taken home. TTL teaches kids to red
 uce\, re-use\, and recycle parts into new projects!\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \
 n \n Day 1 - Monday \n \n \n \n Design using cad software and laser cutter
 s\n\n The kids will brainstorm what type of army they want to pick as team
 s. Each cosplay will be able to be personalised but all require matching H
 elmets and Shields plus a sword/axe/spear ect... No Projectiles!\n\n In th
 e afternoon the kids will learn basic cad modeling on laser control softwa
 re and will be able to design a foam helmet and decorate it.\n\n \n \n \n 
 \n \n Day 2 - Tuesday \n \n \n \n Accessories using 3d printers\n\n We wil
 l allow the kids to create harmless larp weapons or accessories using the 
 shop 3d printers as well as the laser cutters\n\n Kids will learn tinkerca
 d to create a 3d design then learn to slice 3d files before learning to un
 derstand and operate the 3d printers\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Day 3 - Wednesday 
 \n \n \n \n Shields using the wood shop.\n\n Under strict supervision the 
 kids will learn how to use the Miter saw\, Drill press\, Band Saw\, Sander
 \, Nail gun and drill. The morning will be shop training. The afternoon wi
 ll have the kids designing and building shields using their newly aquired 
 skills.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Day 4 - Thursday \n \n \n \n Sewing and leather
 -working.\n\n The kids will decide what accessories will make their cospla
 ys complete. Morning will consist of learning to use a sewing machine and 
 basic use of grommets\, rivets and buckles.\n\n The afternoon will have th
 e kids create their personal customisation such as belts or gauntlets.\n\n
  \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 5  - Friday \n \n \n \n \n Morning will consi
 st of assembling the pieces\, Final fitting and adjustments.\n\n During lu
 nch we will go to the park and film some slow motion live action roleplay 
 battles.\n\n There will be no use of full force or full speed. Damaged cos
 plays will be repaired and the kids will have time to make final use of th
 e makerspace before 3:30 when we will have a photo shoot. Parents are invi
 ted to spectate\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n About Kids Camps at TTLMakerspace 
 \n \n \n We love our young makers at TTLMakerspace\, and run kids programs
  all year long for our active members. Our summer camps provide the opport
 unity for curious young builders to have a very hands-on experience master
 ing tools both traditional and high-tech. \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n \n \n 
 \n\n \n Drop off 8:45 to 9:00 am \n \n \n 9:15  am  skill training \n \n
  \n 10:30 am  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 10:45 am  Building Session 1 \n 
 \n \n 12:00 pm  Lunch (At the Grange Park weather permitting) Kids will b
 e required to bring a lunch and we recommend a re-usable water bottle that
  they can refill during the week. \n \n \n 1:00  pm  Building Session 2 
 \n \n \n 2:30  pm  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 2:45  pm  Building Sessio
