DESCRIPTION:Drag Racing Robot Camp \n\n \n \n Recommended Ages 8-13 \n \n 
 \n\n \n \n \n At the TTL Makerspace we believe that learning should be fun
 \, safe and fun! For a whole week we will study\, design and build remote 
 controlled race cars so we can race them against each other. With a heavy 
 emphasis on safety\, we will empower kids with the confidence and skills n
 eeded to use tools and equipment in a community makerspace.\n\n Participan
 ts will work in teams to design and build a working remote controlled race
  cars. We will Experiment with gears and aerodynamics . We will end the we
 ek with a series of races that parents are encouraged to spectate.\n\n We 
 will experiment with electronics\, robotics\, aerodynamics by learning to 
 use power tools\, soldering irons\, laser cutters and 3d printers.\n\n \n 
 Note: The race cars will be disassembled after the event and can not be ta
 ken home. TTL teaches kids to reduce\, re-use\, and recycle parts into new
  projects!\n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 1 - Monday \n \n \n Electronics 
 and robotics using Soldering Irons\, Hand tools as well as remote transmit
 ters and receivers\n\n The kids will first learn basic circuitry\, motor c
 ontrol then remote control by powering motors and adding gears to achieve 
 various results. The afternoon will have the kids planning and designing t
 he first prototype drive systems as teams.\n\n \n \n \n \n Day 2 - Tuesday
  \n \n \n Race car design using CAD modeling and 3d Printing\n\n The teams
  will learn to create 3d objects\, The software needed to slice it for pri
 nting and finally how 3d printers work the kids will create the first prot
 otype car body and a few wheel designs.\n\n \n \n \n \n Day 3 - Wednesday 
 \n \n \n Aerodynamics using a wind tunnel and laser cutter\n\n We will lea
 rn 2d design and create a wind tunnel as a group using a smoke machine.The
  kids will build a wind tunnel to test the performance of their designs.Wa
 tching footage in slow motion will teach us where improvements can be made
 .\n\n A second prototype will be designed.\n\n \n \n \n \n Day 4 - Thursda
 y \n \n \n Robotics using 3d printing\, Laser cutting and Electronics Tool
 s\n\n The drive system and body will be connected. Various wheel configur
 ations will be tested\n\n Test runs will be allowed in the afternoon\n\n \
 n \n \n \n\n \n \n Day 5  - Friday \n \n \n \n Creating a drag racing rob
 ot with full use of the makerspace\n\n teams will have the morning to make
  final changes and learn to control their robots.\n\n The afternoon will b
 e full of challenges for the robots to complete.\n\n Final races will take
  place Friday at 3:30pm. Parents are encouraged to attend and possibly rec
 ord.\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n About Kids Camps at TTLMakerspace \n \n \n We lo
 ve our young makers at TTLMakerspace\, and run kids programs all year long
  for our active members. Our summer camps provide the opportunity for curi
 ous young builders to have a very hands-on experience mastering tools both
  traditional and high-tech. \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n \n \n \n\n \n Drop o
 ff 8:45 to 9:00 am \n \n \n 9:15  am  skill training \n \n \n 10:30 am 
  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 10:45 am  Building Session 1 \n \n \n 12:00 pm
   Lunch (At the Grange Park weather permitting) Kids will be required to 
 bring a lunch and we recommend a re-usable water bottle that they can refi
 ll during the week. \n \n \n 1:00  pm  Building Session 2 \n \n \n 2:30
   pm  Break and Snacks \n \n \n 2:45  pm  Building Session 3 \n \n \n 
 3:45  pm Cleaning \n \n \n Pick up 4:00 to 4:15 pm with extended care ava
 ilable for an additional fee.
